*> Reads a shapefile (.shp geometry + .dbf attributes) with ShapeLayer and draws it as a map.
*> Real shapefiles are large binary bundles, so this example first writes a tiny synthetic
*> one by hand (two "counties": a plain square and one with a lake-shaped hole) in the ESRI
*> byte layout ShapeLayer::read() expects, then reads it back through the public API.
*> CMD: just TARGET=gis_ex run-cobol
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. GIS-EX.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT BIN-FILE ASSIGN TO BIN-PATH ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
*> Fixed one-byte records: written as raw bytes, with no separators.
FD BIN-FILE.
01 BIN-BYTE PIC X.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".

*> Ring points. Per the ESRI winding convention, outer rings are clockwise and holes
*> counterclockwise. Ring 1 is Lakeside's outline, ring 2 its lake, ring 3 Plainview.
01 POINT-DATA.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 10.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 10.  05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 10.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 10.  05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 3.   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 3.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 4.   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 3.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 4.   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 4.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 3.   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 4.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 3.   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 3.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 10.  05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 10.  05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 10.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 20.  05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 10.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 20.  05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 10.  05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.
01 POINTS REDEFINES POINT-DATA.
   05 PT OCCURS 15.
      10 PT-X USAGE COMP-2.
      10 PT-Y USAGE COMP-2.
*> Each ring is 5 points; shape 1 (Lakeside) has rings 1-2, shape 2 (Plainview) ring 3.
01 SHAPE-DATA.
   05 FILLER PIC 9 VALUE 1.  05 FILLER PIC 9 VALUE 2.
   05 FILLER PIC 9 VALUE 3.  05 FILLER PIC 9 VALUE 1.
01 SHAPES REDEFINES SHAPE-DATA.
   05 SHAPE-ENTRY OCCURS 2.
      10 SHAPE-FIRST-RING PIC 9.
      10 SHAPE-RING-COUNT PIC 9.
78 RING-POINTS VALUE 5.
01 NAME-DATA.
   05 FILLER PIC X(12) VALUE "Lakeside".
   05 FILLER PIC X(12) VALUE "Plainview".
01 NAMES REDEFINES NAME-DATA.
   05 COUNTY-NAME PIC X(12) OCCURS 2.
01 POP-DATA.
   05 FILLER PIC X(8) VALUE "48231".
   05 FILLER PIC X(8) VALUE "19876".
01 POPS REDEFINES POP-DATA.
   05 COUNTY-POP PIC X(8) OCCURS 2.

01 BASE-NAME PIC X(40) VALUE "datamunge_gis_ex_counties_cobol".
01 SVG-PATH  PIC X(40) VALUE "datamunge_gis_ex_map_cobol.svg".

*> The file being built, and typed views for packing numbers into it.
01 BIN-PATH  PIC X(64).
01 FILE-BUF  PIC X(2000).
01 BUF-LEN   USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 BE-INT    PIC S9(9) USAGE BINARY.
01 BE-BYTES  REDEFINES BE-INT PIC X(4).
01 LE-INT    USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 LE-BYTES  REDEFINES LE-INT PIC X(4).
01 LE-SHORT  USAGE BINARY-SHORT UNSIGNED.
01 LE-SHORT-BYTES REDEFINES LE-SHORT PIC X(2).
01 DBL       USAGE COMP-2.
01 DBL-BYTES REDEFINES DBL PIC X(8).
01 MIN-X USAGE COMP-2.
01 MIN-Y USAGE COMP-2.
01 MAX-X USAGE COMP-2.
01 MAX-Y USAGE COMP-2.
01 FIRST-PT  USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 LAST-PT   USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 SHAPE     USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 RING      USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 P         USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 K         USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 FIELD-NAME PIC X(11).
01 FIELD-TYPE PIC X.
01 FIELD-LEN  USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 LENGTH-POS   USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 CONTENT-POS  USAGE BINARY-LONG.

01 COUNTIES   USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 ATTRIBUTES USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 BOUNDS     USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 MAP-PLOT   USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 N-SHAPES   USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 I          USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 NUM-EDIT   PIC Z(18)9.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    PERFORM WRITE-COUNTIES-SHP
    PERFORM WRITE-COUNTIES-DBF

    MOVE BASE-NAME TO DM-SHAPE-LAYER-READ-PATH
    CALL "dm_shape_layer_read" USING DM-SHAPE-LAYER-READ DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-SHAPE-LAYER-READ-RESULT TO COUNTIES

    MOVE COUNTIES TO DM-SHAPE-LAYER-SIZE-SELF
    CALL "dm_shape_layer_size" USING DM-SHAPE-LAYER-SIZE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-SHAPE-LAYER-SIZE-RESULT TO N-SHAPES
    MOVE COUNTIES TO DM-SHAPE-LAYER-SHAPE-TYPE-SELF
    CALL "dm_shape_layer_shape_type" USING DM-SHAPE-LAYER-SHAPE-TYPE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE N-SHAPES TO NUM-EDIT
    DISPLAY "shapes = " FUNCTION TRIM(NUM-EDIT) ", shape_type = "
        DM-SHAPE-LAYER-SHAPE-TYPE-RESULT(1:DM-SHAPE-LAYER-SHAPE-TYPE-RESULT-LENGTH)

    MOVE COUNTIES TO DM-SHAPE-LAYER-BOUNDS-SELF
    CALL "dm_shape_layer_bounds" USING DM-SHAPE-LAYER-BOUNDS DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-SHAPE-LAYER-BOUNDS-RESULT TO BOUNDS
    MOVE BOUNDS TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF
    MOVE 1 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-START
    CALL "dm_vector_double_to_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    DISPLAY "bounds = [" DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) ", " DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
        ", " DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(3) ", " DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(4) "]"
    MOVE BOUNDS TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    DISPLAY " "

    MOVE COUNTIES TO DM-SHAPE-LAYER-ATTRIBUTES-SELF
    CALL "dm_shape_layer_attributes" USING DM-SHAPE-LAYER-ATTRIBUTES DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-SHAPE-LAYER-ATTRIBUTES-RESULT TO ATTRIBUTES
    DISPLAY "attributes"
    MOVE ATTRIBUTES TO DM-DATA-FRAME-TO-STRING-SELF
    CALL "dm_data_frame_to_string" USING DM-DATA-FRAME-TO-STRING DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    DISPLAY DM-DATA-FRAME-TO-STRING-RESULT(1:DM-DATA-FRAME-TO-STRING-RESULT-LENGTH)
    DISPLAY " "

    PERFORM VARYING I FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL I >= N-SHAPES
        MOVE ATTRIBUTES TO DM-DATA-FRAME-STRING-AT-SELF
        MOVE "NAME" TO DM-DATA-FRAME-STRING-AT-COLUMN-NAME
        MOVE I TO DM-DATA-FRAME-STRING-AT-ROW-INDEX
        CALL "dm_data_frame_string_at" USING DM-DATA-FRAME-STRING-AT DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        MOVE COUNTIES TO DM-SHAPE-LAYER-NUM-PARTS-SELF
        MOVE I TO DM-SHAPE-LAYER-NUM-PARTS-SHAPE-INDEX
        CALL "dm_shape_layer_num_parts" USING DM-SHAPE-LAYER-NUM-PARTS DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        MOVE DM-SHAPE-LAYER-NUM-PARTS-RESULT TO NUM-EDIT
        DISPLAY DM-DATA-FRAME-STRING-AT-RESULT(1:DM-DATA-FRAME-STRING-AT-RESULT-LENGTH)
            ": " FUNCTION TRIM(NUM-EDIT) " ring(s)"
    END-PERFORM

    MOVE COUNTIES TO DM-SHAPE-LAYER-PLOT-SELF
    CALL "dm_shape_layer_plot" USING DM-SHAPE-LAYER-PLOT DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-SHAPE-LAYER-PLOT-RESULT TO MAP-PLOT
    MOVE MAP-PLOT TO DM-PLOT-SAVE-SVG-SELF
    MOVE SVG-PATH TO DM-PLOT-SAVE-SVG-PATH
    CALL "dm_plot_save_svg" USING DM-PLOT-SAVE-SVG DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "map saved to " FUNCTION TRIM(SVG-PATH)

    MOVE MAP-PLOT TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE ATTRIBUTES TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE COUNTIES TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
    STOP RUN.

*> The .shp file: a 100-byte header, then one Polygon record per shape.
WRITE-COUNTIES-SHP.
    MOVE 0 TO BUF-LEN
    MOVE 9994 TO BE-INT
    PERFORM PUT-BE-INT
    MOVE 0 TO BE-INT
    PERFORM PUT-BE-INT 5 TIMES
    *> File length in 16-bit words: patched in below, once known.
    PERFORM PUT-BE-INT
    MOVE 1000 TO LE-INT
    PERFORM PUT-LE-INT
    MOVE 5 TO LE-INT
    PERFORM PUT-LE-INT
    MOVE 1 TO FIRST-PT
    MOVE 15 TO LAST-PT
    PERFORM PUT-BOUNDS
    MOVE 0 TO DBL
    PERFORM PUT-DOUBLE 4 TIMES
    PERFORM PUT-POLYGON-RECORD VARYING SHAPE FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL SHAPE > 2
    COMPUTE BE-INT = BUF-LEN / 2
    MOVE BE-BYTES TO FILE-BUF(25:4)
    MOVE SPACES TO BIN-PATH
    STRING FUNCTION TRIM(BASE-NAME) ".shp" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO BIN-PATH
    PERFORM WRITE-BUFFER.

*> A record header (number, content length in words), then the Polygon content.
PUT-POLYGON-RECORD.
    MOVE SHAPE TO BE-INT
    PERFORM PUT-BE-INT
    COMPUTE LENGTH-POS = BUF-LEN + 1
    PERFORM PUT-BE-INT
    MOVE BUF-LEN TO CONTENT-POS
    MOVE 5 TO LE-INT
    PERFORM PUT-LE-INT
    COMPUTE FIRST-PT = (SHAPE-FIRST-RING(SHAPE) - 1) * RING-POINTS + 1
    COMPUTE LAST-PT = FIRST-PT + SHAPE-RING-COUNT(SHAPE) * RING-POINTS - 1
    PERFORM PUT-BOUNDS
    MOVE SHAPE-RING-COUNT(SHAPE) TO LE-INT
    PERFORM PUT-LE-INT
    COMPUTE LE-INT = LAST-PT - FIRST-PT + 1
    PERFORM PUT-LE-INT
    *> Each ring's first point, counted from 0 within the shape.
    PERFORM VARYING RING FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL RING >= SHAPE-RING-COUNT(SHAPE)
        COMPUTE LE-INT = RING * RING-POINTS
        PERFORM PUT-LE-INT
    END-PERFORM
    PERFORM VARYING P FROM FIRST-PT BY 1 UNTIL P > LAST-PT
        MOVE PT-X(P) TO DBL
        PERFORM PUT-DOUBLE
        MOVE PT-Y(P) TO DBL
        PERFORM PUT-DOUBLE
    END-PERFORM
    COMPUTE BE-INT = (BUF-LEN - CONTENT-POS) / 2
    MOVE BE-BYTES TO FILE-BUF(LENGTH-POS:4).

*> The bounding box (xmin, ymin, xmax, ymax) of points FIRST-PT to LAST-PT.
PUT-BOUNDS.
    MOVE PT-X(FIRST-PT) TO MIN-X MAX-X
    MOVE PT-Y(FIRST-PT) TO MIN-Y MAX-Y
    PERFORM VARYING P FROM FIRST-PT BY 1 UNTIL P > LAST-PT
        IF PT-X(P) < MIN-X MOVE PT-X(P) TO MIN-X END-IF
        IF PT-X(P) > MAX-X MOVE PT-X(P) TO MAX-X END-IF
        IF PT-Y(P) < MIN-Y MOVE PT-Y(P) TO MIN-Y END-IF
        IF PT-Y(P) > MAX-Y MOVE PT-Y(P) TO MAX-Y END-IF
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE MIN-X TO DBL
    PERFORM PUT-DOUBLE
    MOVE MIN-Y TO DBL
    PERFORM PUT-DOUBLE
    MOVE MAX-X TO DBL
    PERFORM PUT-DOUBLE
    MOVE MAX-Y TO DBL
    PERFORM PUT-DOUBLE.

*> The .dbf file: header, NAME (C, 12) and POP (N, 8) field descriptors, then records.
WRITE-COUNTIES-DBF.
    MOVE 0 TO BUF-LEN
    MOVE X"03000000" TO FILE-BUF(1:4)
    MOVE 4 TO BUF-LEN
    MOVE 2 TO LE-INT
    PERFORM PUT-LE-INT
    *> Header size 32 + 2 * 32 + 1, record size 1 + 12 + 8.
    MOVE 97 TO LE-SHORT
    PERFORM PUT-LE-SHORT
    MOVE 21 TO LE-SHORT
    PERFORM PUT-LE-SHORT
    MOVE 20 TO K
    PERFORM PUT-ZEROS
    MOVE "NAME" TO FIELD-NAME
    MOVE "C" TO FIELD-TYPE
    MOVE 12 TO FIELD-LEN
    PERFORM PUT-FIELD
    MOVE "POP" TO FIELD-NAME
    MOVE "N" TO FIELD-TYPE
    MOVE 8 TO FIELD-LEN
    PERFORM PUT-FIELD
    MOVE X"0D" TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 1:1)
    ADD 1 TO BUF-LEN
    PERFORM VARYING SHAPE FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL SHAPE > 2
        MOVE " " TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 1:1)
        MOVE COUNTY-NAME(SHAPE) TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 2:12)
        MOVE COUNTY-POP(SHAPE) TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 14:8)
        ADD 21 TO BUF-LEN
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE SPACES TO BIN-PATH
    STRING FUNCTION TRIM(BASE-NAME) ".dbf" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO BIN-PATH
    PERFORM WRITE-BUFFER.

*> A 32-byte field descriptor: name (11 bytes, zero-padded), type, 4 zeros, length, 15 zeros.
PUT-FIELD.
    MOVE LOW-VALUES TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 1:32)
    MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(FIELD-NAME) TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 1:FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(FIELD-NAME)))
    MOVE FIELD-TYPE TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 12:1)
    MOVE FIELD-LEN TO LE-SHORT
    MOVE LE-SHORT-BYTES(1:1) TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 17:1)
    ADD 32 TO BUF-LEN.

PUT-BE-INT.
    MOVE BE-BYTES TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 1:4)
    ADD 4 TO BUF-LEN.

PUT-LE-INT.
    MOVE LE-BYTES TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 1:4)
    ADD 4 TO BUF-LEN.

PUT-LE-SHORT.
    MOVE LE-SHORT-BYTES TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 1:2)
    ADD 2 TO BUF-LEN.

PUT-DOUBLE.
    MOVE DBL-BYTES TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 1:8)
    ADD 8 TO BUF-LEN.

*> K zero bytes.
PUT-ZEROS.
    MOVE LOW-VALUES TO FILE-BUF(BUF-LEN + 1:K)
    ADD K TO BUF-LEN.

*> Writes the first BUF-LEN bytes of FILE-BUF to BIN-PATH.
WRITE-BUFFER.
    OPEN OUTPUT BIN-FILE
    PERFORM VARYING K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL K > BUF-LEN
        MOVE FILE-BUF(K:1) TO BIN-BYTE
        WRITE BIN-BYTE
    END-PERFORM
    CLOSE BIN-FILE.

*> Stops with the error after a failed call.
CHECK.
    IF NOT DM-STATUS-OK
        DISPLAY "datamunge error (" FUNCTION TRIM(DM-STATUS-KIND) "): "
            DM-STATUS-MESSAGE(1:DM-STATUS-LENGTH) UPON SYSERR
        STOP RUN RETURNING 1
    END-IF.
